From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Default the copy and move members of ParquetString

ParquetString pulls in the assignment operators of its basic_string base
with `using base::operator=;`. GCC 10 (Rtools42) counts the base's
copy assignment brought in that way as a user-provided copy assignment
of ParquetString itself and reports -Wdeprecated-copy wherever the
Thrift-generated code in parquet_types.cpp assigns one ParquetString
to another, at 19 sites. GCC 11 and later do not.

Declaring the copy and move constructors and assignment operators as
defaulted states what the compiler generated anyway, so nothing changes
at run time and no compiler has anything left to infer.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
 src/duckdb/third_party/parquet/parquet_arena.h | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/third_party/parquet/parquet_arena.h b/src/duckdb/third_party/parquet/parquet_arena.h
index fa8fa3f7cf..25a50f7210 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/third_party/parquet/parquet_arena.h
+++ b/src/duckdb/third_party/parquet/parquet_arena.h
@@ -73,6 +73,11 @@ public:
 	using base::base;
 	using base::operator=;
 
+	ParquetString(const ParquetString &other) = default;
+	ParquetString(ParquetString &&other) = default;
+	ParquetString &operator=(const ParquetString &other) = default;
+	ParquetString &operator=(ParquetString &&other) = default;
+
 	ParquetString &operator=(const std::string &value) {
 		assign(value.data(), value.size());
 		return *this;
